<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE topic PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Topic//EN" "topic.dtd">
<topic id="ai_positron_enterprise-hooks">
  <title>Intercepting AI Events Using Hooks</title>
  <body>
    <p id="p_hooks_intro_a1b">The <b>Oxygen AI Positron</b> add-on exposes a hook system that lets
      developers intercept events fired during the AI lifecycle. A hook handler can observe
        <i>fire-and-forget</i> events for auditing or analytics, or veto blocking events to prevent
      an action from running.</p>
    <p id="p_hooks_usecases_b2c">Typical use cases include:</p>
    <ul id="ul_hooks_usecases_c3d">
      <li id="li_hooks_uc_audit">Auditing every AI action, tool call, or shell command to an
        external log or compliance system.</li>
      <li id="li_hooks_uc_gate">Gating risky operations (for example, blocking shell commands that
        modify production files).</li>
      <li id="li_hooks_uc_subagent">Controlling sub-agent execution to enforce organizational
        policies on autonomous AI tasks.</li>
      <li id="li_hooks_uc_metrics">Collecting token usage metrics after each assistant turn.</li>
    </ul>
    <section id="section_hooks_impl">
      <title>Implementing a Hook Handler</title>
      <p id="p_hooks_impl_a">To create a hook handler add-on, follow these steps:</p>
      <ol id="ol_hooks_impl_steps">
        <li id="li_hooks_dep">Add <codeph>oxygen-ai-positron-api</codeph> as a provided dependency
          in your plugin project's
            <filepath>pom.xml</filepath>:<codeblock id="codeblock_hooks_dep" outputclass="language-xml">&lt;dependency>
  &lt;groupId>com.oxygenxml&lt;/groupId>
  &lt;artifactId>oxygen-ai-positron-api&lt;/artifactId>
  &lt;version>8.3.0&lt;/version>
  &lt;scope>provided&lt;/scope>
&lt;/dependency></codeblock><p id="p_hooks_repo">The artifact is published at <xref
              href="https://oxygenxml.com/maven/" format="html" scope="external"
                ><b>https://oxygenxml.com/maven/</b></xref>. Add the repository to your
              <filepath>pom.xml</filepath> (if it is not already
            present):<codeblock id="codeblock_hooks_repo" outputclass="language-xml">&lt;repository>
  &lt;id>oxygen-public-repo&lt;/id>
  &lt;url>https://www.oxygenxml.com/maven/&lt;/url>
&lt;/repository></codeblock></p></li>
        <li id="li_hooks_implement">Implement the
            <codeph>com.oxygenxml.positron.api.hook.AIHooksHandler</codeph> interface in your
          plugin's libraries. The single method <codeph>eventOccurred(AIHookEvent event, String
            eventPayload)</codeph> is called for every hook event. Throw an exception from this
          method to <b>veto</b> a blocking event and prevent the associated action from
          running.<codeblock id="codeblock_hooks_example" outputclass="language-java">package my.pack;

import java.util.List;

import com.fasterxml.jackson.databind.ObjectMapper;
import com.oxygenxml.positron.api.hook.AIHookEvent;
import com.oxygenxml.positron.api.hook.AIHooksHandler;
import com.oxygenxml.positron.api.hook.payload.BeforeShellExecutionPayload;

/**
 * Hook handler that blocks shell commands considered dangerous for
 * a documentation project (destructive file operations, package
 * installations, and network-fetching utilities).
 */
public class ShellGuardHooksHandler implements AIHooksHandler {

  private static final ObjectMapper MAPPER = new ObjectMapper();

  private static final List&lt;String> BLOCKED_PATTERNS = List.of(
      "rm ",  "rmdir", "del ",  "rd ",
      "npm install", "pip install", "mvn install",
      "curl", "wget"
  );

  @Override
  public void eventOccurred(AIHookEvent event, String eventPayload) throws Exception {
    if (event == AIHookEvent.BEFORE_SHELL_EXECUTION) {
      blockDangerousCommands(eventPayload);
    }
  }

  private void blockDangerousCommands(String payload) throws Exception {
    BeforeShellExecutionPayload data = MAPPER.readValue(payload, BeforeShellExecutionPayload.class);
    String command = data.getCommand();
    if (command == null) {
      return;
    }
    String lowerCommand = command.toLowerCase();
    for (String pattern : BLOCKED_PATTERNS) {
      if (lowerCommand.contains(pattern)) {
        throw new Exception(
            "Shell command blocked by policy: '" + command + "'. "
            + "Matched restricted pattern: '" + pattern + "'."
        );
      }
    }
  }
}</codeblock></li>
        <li id="li_hooks_ext_point">In the plugin descriptor file, declare the extension point that
          points to your implementation:
          <codeblock id="codeblock_hooks_ext" xml:space="preserve" outputclass="language-xml">&lt;extension type="AIHooksHandler" class="my.pack.AuditHooksHandler"/&gt;</codeblock></li>
      </ol>
    </section>
    <section id="section_hooks_events">
      <title>Hook Events Reference</title>
      <p id="p_hooks_events_intro">The following tables list all events defined in
          <codeph>AIHookEvent</codeph>, grouped by lifecycle category. Events marked as
          <b>Blocking</b> can be vetoed by throwing an exception inside
          <codeph>eventOccurred</codeph>. Events marked as <b>Fire-and-forget</b> are informational
        (throwing an exception has no effect on the AI action).</p>
      <p id="p_hooks_payload_base">Every event delivers its data as a JSON string. All payloads
        share the following base fields, inherited from <codeph>BaseHookPayload</codeph>:</p>
      <simpletable id="simpletable_base_payload" relcolwidth="1* 1* 2*">
        <sthead>
          <stentry>Field</stentry>
          <stentry>Type</stentry>
          <stentry>Description</stentry>
        </sthead>
        <strow>
          <stentry><codeph>sessionId</codeph></stentry>
          <stentry>string</stentry>
          <stentry>Stable identifier for the current chat session, constant across all
            turns.</stentry>
        </strow>
        <strow>
          <stentry><codeph>actionOrAgentId</codeph></stentry>
          <stentry>string</stentry>
          <stentry>Identifier of the AI action or agent (chat mode) that produced this event (e.g.
              <codeph>agent</codeph>, <codeph>ask</codeph>, or a custom chat mode ID).</stentry>
        </strow>
        <strow>
          <stentry><codeph>generationId</codeph></stentry>
          <stentry>string</stentry>
          <stentry>Identifier that changes with each user message / AI generation round.</stentry>
        </strow>
        <strow>
          <stentry><codeph>connectionId</codeph></stentry>
          <stentry>string</stentry>
          <stentry>Identifier of the AI connection as configured by the user in
            Preferences.</stentry>
        </strow>
        <strow>
          <stentry><codeph>model</codeph></stentry>
          <stentry>string</stentry>
          <stentry>The AI model currently in use (e.g. <codeph>claude-opus-4-7</codeph>).</stentry>
        </strow>
        <strow>
          <stentry><codeph>hookEventName</codeph></stentry>
          <stentry>string</stentry>
          <stentry>The name of the hook event that fired (e.g.
            <codeph>beforeShellExecution</codeph>).</stentry>
        </strow>
        <strow>
          <stentry><codeph>positronVersion</codeph></stentry>
          <stentry>string</stentry>
          <stentry>Running version of the AI Positron plugin (e.g.
            <codeph>8.3.0</codeph>).</stentry>
        </strow>
        <strow>
          <stentry><codeph>oxygenVersion</codeph></stentry>
          <stentry>string</stentry>
          <stentry>Running version of the host application (e.g.
            <codeph>27.1.0</codeph>).</stentry>
        </strow>
        <strow>
          <stentry><codeph>oxygenDistribution</codeph></stentry>
          <stentry>string</stentry>
          <stentry>Host product distribution (e.g. <codeph>Oxygen XML Editor</codeph>).</stentry>
        </strow>
        <strow>
          <stentry><codeph>workspaceRoot</codeph></stentry>
          <stentry>string</stentry>
          <stentry>Absolute path to the current project or workspace root.</stentry>
        </strow>
        <strow>
          <stentry><codeph>userId</codeph></stentry>
          <stentry>string</stentry>
          <stentry>System identifier of the user.</stentry>
        </strow>
      </simpletable>
      <p><dl id="dl_hooks_events">
          <dlentry id="dlentry_session_start">
            <dt><codeph>sessionStart</codeph>: Fire-and-forget</dt>
            <dd>Fired when a new chat conversation is created.</dd>
            <dd>
              <simpletable id="st_session_start" relcolwidth="1* 1* 2*">
                <sthead>
                  <stentry>Field</stentry>
                  <stentry>Type</stentry>
                  <stentry>Description</stentry>
                </sthead>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>actionName</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>Human-readable name of the AI action that started the session.</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>backgroundAgent</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>boolean</stentry>
                  <stentry>Present and <codeph>true</codeph> when the session was started by an
                    autonomous background agent rather than a direct user interaction. Omitted
                    when <codeph>false</codeph>.</stentry>
                </strow>
              </simpletable>
            </dd>
          </dlentry>
          
          <dlentry id="dlentry_session_end">
            <dt><codeph>sessionEnd</codeph>: Fire-and-forget</dt>
            <dd>Fired when a chat conversation is closed or cleared. </dd>
            <dd>
              <simpletable id="st_session_end" relcolwidth="1* 1* 2*">
                <sthead>
                  <stentry>Field</stentry>
                  <stentry>Type</stentry>
                  <stentry>Description</stentry>
                </sthead>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>reason</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>Reason the session ended: <codeph>user_close</codeph> or
                    <codeph>application_close</codeph>.</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>backgroundAgent</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>boolean</stentry>
                  <stentry>Present and <codeph>true</codeph> when the session was started by a
                    background agent. Omitted from JSON when <codeph>false</codeph>.</stentry>
                </strow>
              </simpletable>
            </dd>
          </dlentry>
          
          <dlentry id="dlentry_session_reload">
            <dt><codeph>sessionReload</codeph>: Fire-and-forget</dt>
            <dd>Fired when the user restores a previous conversation from the chat history.</dd>
            <dd>
              <simpletable id="st_session_reload" relcolwidth="1* 1* 2*">
                <sthead>
                  <stentry>Field</stentry>
                  <stentry>Type</stentry>
                  <stentry>Description</stentry>
                </sthead>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>actionName</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>Human-readable name of the AI action that was active when this session was
                    originally created.</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>backgroundAgent</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>boolean</stentry>
                  <stentry>Present and <codeph>true</codeph> when the session was originally started
                    by a background agent. Omitted from JSON when <codeph>false</codeph>.</stentry>
                </strow>
              </simpletable>
            </dd>
          </dlentry>
          
          <dlentry id="dlentry_before_start_action">
            <dt><codeph>beforeStartAction</codeph> : Blocking</dt>
            <dd>Fired before an AI action is launched. Throwing an exception vetoes the action and
              prevents it from running. The action identifier is available via the base field
                <codeph>actionOrAgentId</codeph>.</dd>
            <dd>
              <simpletable id="st_before_start_action" relcolwidth="1* 1* 2*">
                <sthead>
                  <stentry>Field</stentry>
                  <stentry>Type</stentry>
                  <stentry>Description</stentry>
                </sthead>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>inputContent</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>The text content of the initial user input passed to the action.</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>inputAttachments</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string[]</stentry>
                  <stentry>URLs of attachments included in the initial user input. Omitted when
                    empty.</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>tools</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string[]</stentry>
                  <stentry>IDs of the tools available to the model for this request. Omitted when
                    empty.</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>actionExpandParameters</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>map</stentry>
                  <stentry>Expanded runtime parameters used to invoke the action (key-value pairs).
                    Omitted when empty.</stentry>
                </strow>
              </simpletable>
            </dd>
          </dlentry>
          
          <dlentry id="dlentry_before_submit_prompt">
            <dt><codeph>beforeSubmitPrompt</codeph> : Blocking</dt>
            <dd>Fired right before a user prompt is submitted to the AI model from the chat UI.
              Throwing an exception prevents the prompt from being sent.</dd>
            <dd>
              <simpletable id="st_before_submit_prompt" relcolwidth="1* 1* 2*">
                <sthead>
                  <stentry>Field</stentry>
                  <stentry>Type</stentry>
                  <stentry>Description</stentry>
                </sthead>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>prompt</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>The full text of the prompt the user is about to submit.</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>attachments</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string[]</stentry>
                  <stentry>URLs of attachments included by user. Omitted when empty.</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>tools</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string[]</stentry>
                  <stentry>IDs of the tools available to the model for this request. Omitted when
                    empty.</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>actionExpandParameters</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>map</stentry>
                  <stentry>Expanded runtime parameters used to invoke the action (key-value pairs).
                    Omitted when empty.</stentry>
                </strow>
              </simpletable>
            </dd>
          </dlentry>
          
          <dlentry id="dlentry_agent_finish">
            <dt><codeph>agentFinish</codeph>: Fire-and-forget</dt>
            <dd>Fired when the AI agent interaction finishes, regardless of whether it completed
              successfully, was aborted by the user, or terminated by an error.</dd>
            <dd>
              <simpletable id="st_agent_finish" relcolwidth="1* 1* 2*">
                <sthead>
                  <stentry>Field</stentry>
                  <stentry>Type</stentry>
                  <stentry>Description</stentry>
                </sthead>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>status</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>Reason the interaction ended: <codeph>completed</codeph>,
                    <codeph>aborted</codeph>, or <codeph>error</codeph>.</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>toolCallRounds</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>integer</stentry>
                  <stentry>Number of tool-call rounds completed during the interaction (0 for plain
                    Q&amp;A with no tools).</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>errorMessage</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>Human-readable error description. Present only when
                    <codeph>status</codeph> is <codeph>error</codeph>.</stentry>
                </strow>
              </simpletable>
            </dd>
          </dlentry>
          <dlentry id="dlentry_pre_tool_use">
            <dt><codeph>preToolUse</codeph> : Blocking</dt>
            <dd>Fired before any AI tool (function or action) is invoked. Throwing an exception
              prevents the tool from running.</dd>
            <dd>
              <simpletable id="st_pre_tool_use" relcolwidth="1* 1* 2*">
                <sthead>
                  <stentry>Field</stentry>
                  <stentry>Type</stentry>
                  <stentry>Description</stentry>
                </sthead>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>toolId</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>ID of the tool about to be invoked (e.g.
                    <codeph>invoke_cmd_line</codeph>).</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>toolInput</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>JSON object</stentry>
                  <stentry>Tool arguments as a raw JSON object.</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>toolUseId</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>Unique identifier for this specific tool call, assigned by the AI
                    model.</stentry>
                </strow>
              </simpletable>
            </dd>
          </dlentry>
          
          <dlentry id="dlentry_post_tool_use">
            <dt><codeph>postToolUse</codeph>: Fire-and-forget</dt>
            <dd>Fired after a tool has completed successfully. Use it for auditing, analytics, or
              collecting tool execution metrics.</dd>
            <dd>
              <simpletable id="st_post_tool_use" relcolwidth="1* 1* 2*">
                <sthead>
                  <stentry>Field</stentry>
                  <stentry>Type</stentry>
                  <stentry>Description</stentry>
                </sthead>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>toolName</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>Name of the tool that was invoked.</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>toolInput</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>JSON object</stentry>
                  <stentry>Tool arguments as a raw JSON object.</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>toolOutput</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>Output produced by the tool execution.</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>toolUseId</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>Unique identifier for this specific tool call, assigned by the AI
                    model.</stentry>
                </strow>
              </simpletable>
            </dd>
          </dlentry>
          
          <dlentry id="dlentry_post_tool_use_failure">
            <dt><codeph>postToolUseFailure</codeph>: Fire-and-forget</dt>
            <dd>Fired after a tool invocation has failed, timed out, or was denied.</dd>
            <dd>
              <simpletable id="st_post_tool_use_failure" relcolwidth="1* 1* 2*">
                <sthead>
                  <stentry>Field</stentry>
                  <stentry>Type</stentry>
                  <stentry>Description</stentry>
                </sthead>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>toolName</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>Name of the tool that failed.</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>toolInput</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>JSON object</stentry>
                  <stentry>Tool arguments as a raw JSON object.</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>toolUseId</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>Unique identifier for this specific tool call, assigned by the AI
                    model.</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>errorMessage</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>Human-readable description of the failure.</stentry>
                </strow>
              </simpletable>
            </dd>
          </dlentry>
          <dlentry id="dlentry_subagent_start">
            <dt><codeph>subagentStart</codeph> : Blocking</dt>
            <dd>Fired before a sub-agent or sub-action is started. Throwing an exception prevents the
              sub-agent from being created.</dd>
            <dd>
              <simpletable id="st_subagent_start" relcolwidth="1* 1* 2*">
                <sthead>
                  <stentry>Field</stentry>
                  <stentry>Type</stentry>
                  <stentry>Description</stentry>
                </sthead>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>subActionOrAgentId</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>Identifier of the sub-action or sub-agent being started (e.g.
                    <codeph>improve-readability</codeph>).</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>actionName</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>Human-readable name of the sub-action or sub-agent.</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>content</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>The document content or text fragment that the sub-agent will
                    process.</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>parentSessionId</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>Session ID of the parent agent that spawned this sub-agent.</stentry>
                </strow>
              </simpletable>
            </dd>
          </dlentry>
          
          <dlentry id="dlentry_subagent_stop">
            <dt><codeph>subagentStop</codeph>: Fire-and-forget</dt>
            <dd>Fired when a sub-agent finishes, errors, or is abandoned.</dd>
            <dd>
              <simpletable id="st_subagent_stop" relcolwidth="1* 1* 2*">
                <sthead>
                  <stentry>Field</stentry>
                  <stentry>Type</stentry>
                  <stentry>Description</stentry>
                </sthead>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>subActionOrAgentId</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>Identifier of the sub-action or sub-agent that ended.</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>actionName</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>Human-readable name of the sub-action.</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>status</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>Outcome of the sub-agent: <codeph>completed</codeph> or
                      <codeph>failed</codeph>.</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>durationMs</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>long</stentry>
                  <stentry>Total wall-clock duration of the sub-agent execution in
                    milliseconds.</stentry>
                </strow>
              </simpletable>
            </dd>
          </dlentry>
          <dlentry id="dlentry_before_shell">
            <dt><codeph>beforeShellExecution</codeph> : Blocking</dt>
            <dd>Fired before a shell command is executed by the AI agent. Throwing an exception
              prevents the command from running. This is the primary hook to use when enforcing shell
              command policies.</dd>
            <dd>
              <simpletable id="st_before_shell" relcolwidth="1* 1* 2*">
                <sthead>
                  <stentry>Field</stentry>
                  <stentry>Type</stentry>
                  <stentry>Description</stentry>
                </sthead>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>command</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>The full shell command string about to be executed.</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>timeoutSeconds</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>integer</stentry>
                  <stentry>Maximum allowed execution time in seconds. Absent if no limit is
                    set.</stentry>
                </strow>
              </simpletable>
            </dd>
          </dlentry>
          
          <dlentry id="dlentry_after_shell">
            <dt><codeph>afterShellExecution</codeph>: Fire-and-forget</dt>
            <dd>Fired after a shell command has finished executing. Use it for auditing or collecting
              metrics from command output.</dd>
            <dd>
              <simpletable id="st_after_shell" relcolwidth="1* 1* 2*">
                <sthead>
                  <stentry>Field</stentry>
                  <stentry>Type</stentry>
                  <stentry>Description</stentry>
                </sthead>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>command</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>The shell command that was executed.</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>output</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>Combined stdout/stderr output of the command.</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>exitCode</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>integer</stentry>
                  <stentry>Process exit code, or absent if the process was terminated
                    abnormally.</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>durationMs</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>long</stentry>
                  <stentry>Wall-clock duration of the command execution in milliseconds.</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>succeeded</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>boolean</stentry>
                  <stentry><codeph>true</codeph> if the command ran without a system-level error
                    regardless of the process exit code; <codeph>false</codeph> if execution failed
                    before the process could complete (e.g. IOException, unsupported
                    platform).</stentry>
                </strow>
              </simpletable>
            </dd>
          </dlentry>
          <dlentry id="dlentry_before_mcp">
            <dt><codeph>beforeMCPExecution</codeph> : Blocking</dt>
            <dd>Fired before an MCP (Model Context Protocol) tool is invoked. Throwing an exception
              prevents the tool from running.</dd>
            <dd>
              <simpletable id="st_before_mcp" relcolwidth="1* 1* 2*">
                <sthead>
                  <stentry>Field</stentry>
                  <stentry>Type</stentry>
                  <stentry>Description</stentry>
                </sthead>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>serverName</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>Name of the MCP server hosting the tool.</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>toolName</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>Name of the MCP tool to be invoked.</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>toolInput</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>JSON object</stentry>
                  <stentry>Tool arguments as a raw JSON object.</stentry>
                </strow>
              </simpletable>
            </dd>
          </dlentry>
          
          <dlentry id="dlentry_after_mcp">
            <dt><codeph>afterMCPExecution</codeph>: Fire-and-forget</dt>
            <dd>Fired after an MCP tool execution completes, whether successfully or with an error.
              Includes the tool's input parameters, the JSON result, and the execution
              outcome.</dd>
            <dd>
              <simpletable id="st_after_mcp" relcolwidth="1* 1* 2*">
                <sthead>
                  <stentry>Field</stentry>
                  <stentry>Type</stentry>
                  <stentry>Description</stentry>
                </sthead>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>serverName</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>Name of the MCP server that hosted the tool.</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>toolName</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>Name of the MCP tool that was invoked.</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>toolInput</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>JSON object</stentry>
                  <stentry>Tool arguments as a raw JSON object.</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>resultJson</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>JSON value</stentry>
                  <stentry>Result returned by the MCP tool as a raw JSON value. Absent when the
                    execution failed.</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>succeeded</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>boolean</stentry>
                  <stentry><codeph>true</codeph> if the MCP tool completed successfully;
                      <codeph>false</codeph> if it threw an error.</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>errorMessage</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>Human-readable description of the failure. Absent when
                      <codeph>succeeded</codeph> is <codeph>true</codeph>.</stentry>
                </strow>
              </simpletable>
            </dd>
          </dlentry>
          <dlentry id="dlentry_before_read_file">
            <dt><codeph>beforeReadFile</codeph> : Blocking</dt>
            <dd>Fired before the agent reads a file. Throwing an exception blocks the agent's access
              to that file. Use this hook to implement file-level access control (for example, to
              prevent the AI from reading files that contain secrets).</dd>
            <dd>
              <simpletable id="st_before_read_file" relcolwidth="1* 1* 2*">
                <sthead>
                  <stentry>Field</stentry>
                  <stentry>Type</stentry>
                  <stentry>Description</stentry>
                </sthead>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>filePath</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>Absolute path or URL of the file about to be read.</stentry>
                </strow>
              </simpletable>
            </dd>
          </dlentry>

          <dlentry id="dlentry_after_read_file">
            <dt><codeph>afterReadFile</codeph>: Fire-and-forget</dt>
            <dd>Fired after the agent successfully reads a file. Use it to audit file-access
              patterns or log the content retrieved by the agent.</dd>
            <dd>
              <simpletable id="st_after_read_file" relcolwidth="1* 1* 2*">
                <sthead>
                  <stentry>Field</stentry>
                  <stentry>Type</stentry>
                  <stentry>Description</stentry>
                </sthead>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>filePath</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>Absolute path or URL of the file that was read.</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>content</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>The content that was read from the file.</stentry>
                </strow>
              </simpletable>
            </dd>
          </dlentry>

          <dlentry id="dlentry_before_edit_file">
            <dt><codeph>beforeEditFile</codeph> : Blocking</dt>
            <dd>Fired before the agent edits or creates a file. Throwing an exception prevents the
              write from happening (the exception message is returned to the AI model as an
                error).<note id="note_ltc_dxg_3jc">The event is only fired when the content to be
                written has been successfully computed. For replacement-based edits, this means the
                replacement strings were located in the existing file content.</note></dd>
            <dd>
              <simpletable id="st_before_edit_file" relcolwidth="1* 1* 2*">
                <sthead>
                  <stentry>Field</stentry>
                  <stentry>Type</stentry>
                  <stentry>Description</stentry>
                </sthead>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>filePath</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>Absolute path or URL of the file about to be modified or
                    created.</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>operation</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>Type of operation about to be performed: <codeph>create</codeph> or
                    <codeph>edit</codeph>.</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>content</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>The full content that will be written to the file.</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>fragments</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>object[]</stentry>
                  <stentry>The individual text replacements about to be applied. Each fragment
                    contains an <codeph>oldValue</codeph> and a <codeph>newValue</codeph>. Absent
                    when the entire file content will be written at once.</stentry>
                </strow>
              </simpletable>
            </dd>
          </dlentry>

          <dlentry id="dlentry_after_edit_file">
            <dt><codeph>afterEditFile</codeph>: Fire-and-forget</dt>
            <dd>Fired after the agent attempts to edit or create a file, both on success and on
              failure. Use it to audit AI-generated file changes.</dd>
            <dd>
              <simpletable id="st_after_edit_file" relcolwidth="1* 1* 2*">
                <sthead>
                  <stentry>Field</stentry>
                  <stentry>Type</stentry>
                  <stentry>Description</stentry>
                </sthead>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>filePath</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>Absolute path or URL of the file that was modified or created.</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>operation</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>Type of operation performed: <codeph>create</codeph> or
                    <codeph>edit</codeph>.</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>content</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>The complete file content after a successful write, or
                    <codeph>null</codeph> when the write failed. For fragment-based edits this is
                    the full document with all replacements already merged in.</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>toolResult</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>The result string returned to the AI model after the tool call completed
                    (e.g. a success confirmation or an error message).</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>succeeded</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>boolean</stentry>
                  <stentry><codeph>true</codeph> when the file was written to disk successfully,
                    <codeph>false</codeph> when the save failed.</stentry>
                </strow>
              </simpletable>
            </dd>
          </dlentry>
          
          <dlentry id="dlentry_after_agent_response">
            <dt><codeph>afterAgentResponse</codeph>: Fire-and-forget</dt>
            <dd>Fired after the agent completes an assistant turn, whether the turn contained only
              tool calls or produced a visible text response.</dd>
            <dd>
              <simpletable id="st_after_agent_response" relcolwidth="1* 1* 2*">
                <sthead>
                  <stentry>Field</stentry>
                  <stentry>Type</stentry>
                  <stentry>Description</stentry>
                </sthead>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>response</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>The text content of the completed assistant turn. Empty string when the
                    turn consisted solely of tool calls.</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>toolCallNames</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string[]</stentry>
                  <stentry>Names of the tools called in this turn. Omitted when empty.</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>tokensUsage</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>object</stentry>
                  <stentry>Token usage information for this assistant turn. Omitted when not reported
                    by the backend.</stentry>
                </strow>
              </simpletable>
            </dd>
          </dlentry>
          
          <dlentry id="dlentry_after_agent_thought">
            <dt><codeph>afterAgentThought</codeph>: Fire-and-forget</dt>
            <dd>Fired after the agent completes a thinking block (extended thinking mode). Use it to
              observe the agent's reasoning process.</dd>
            <dd>
              <simpletable id="st_after_agent_thought" relcolwidth="1* 1* 2*">
                <sthead>
                  <stentry>Field</stentry>
                  <stentry>Type</stentry>
                  <stentry>Description</stentry>
                </sthead>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>text</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>The thinking/reasoning text. Depending on the model it may be a summary or
                    the complete text.</stentry>
                </strow>
              </simpletable>
            </dd>
          </dlentry>
          
          <dlentry id="dlentry_after_user_insert">
            <dt><codeph>afterUserInsertResponse</codeph>: Fire-and-forget</dt>
            <dd>Fired after the user clicks the
                <uicontrol>Insert</uicontrol>/<uicontrol>Replace</uicontrol> button in the chat
              panel to apply an AI suggestion in the document.</dd>
            <dd>
              <simpletable id="st_after_user_insert" relcolwidth="1* 1* 2*">
                <sthead>
                  <stentry>Field</stentry>
                  <stentry>Type</stentry>
                  <stentry>Description</stentry>
                </sthead>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>content</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>The content that was inserted or used to replace the selection.</stentry>
                </strow>
              </simpletable>
            </dd>
          </dlentry>
          
          <dlentry id="dlentry_after_user_preview">
            <dt><codeph>afterUserPreviewResponse</codeph>: Fire-and-forget</dt>
            <dd>Fired after the user clicks the <uicontrol>Preview</uicontrol> button in the chat
              panel and the preview dialog closes. The preview opens a diff view comparing the
              current editor content with the result of applying the AI response, so the user can
              review the changes before deciding whether to apply them.</dd>
            <dd>
              <simpletable id="st_after_user_preview" relcolwidth="1* 1* 2*">
                <sthead>
                  <stentry>Field</stentry>
                  <stentry>Type</stentry>
                  <stentry>Description</stentry>
                </sthead>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>content</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>The content that was sent to the preview dialog.</stentry>
                </strow>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>applied</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>boolean</stentry>
                  <stentry><codeph>true</codeph> if the user applied the changes from within the
                    preview dialog; <codeph>false</codeph> if the dialog was closed without
                    applying.</stentry>
                </strow>
              </simpletable>
            </dd>
          </dlentry>

          <dlentry id="dlentry_after_copy_response">
            <dt><codeph>afterCopyResponse</codeph>: Fire-and-forget</dt>
            <dd>Fired after the user clicks the <uicontrol>Copy</uicontrol> button in the chat
              panel to copy an AI response to the clipboard.</dd>
            <dd>
              <simpletable id="st_after_copy_response" relcolwidth="1* 1* 2*">
                <sthead>
                  <stentry>Field</stentry>
                  <stentry>Type</stentry>
                  <stentry>Description</stentry>
                </sthead>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>content</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string</stentry>
                  <stentry>The text that was copied to the system clipboard.</stentry>
                </strow>
              </simpletable>
            </dd>
          </dlentry>

          <dlentry id="dlentry_after_user_accept">
            <dt><codeph>afterUserAcceptChanges</codeph>: Fire-and-forget</dt>
            <dd>Fired after the user accepts agentic file changes proposed by the AI agent.</dd>
            <dd>
              <simpletable id="st_after_user_accept" relcolwidth="1* 1* 2*">
                <sthead>
                  <stentry>Field</stentry>
                  <stentry>Type</stentry>
                  <stentry>Description</stentry>
                </sthead>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>documents</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string[]</stentry>
                  <stentry>List of absolute paths or URLs of the documents whose changes were
                    accepted.</stentry>
                </strow>
              </simpletable>
            </dd>
          </dlentry>
          
          <dlentry id="dlentry_after_user_reject">
            <dt><codeph>afterUserRejectChanges</codeph>: Fire-and-forget</dt>
            <dd>Fired after the user rejects agentic file changes proposed by the AI agent.</dd>
            <dd>
              <simpletable id="st_after_user_reject" relcolwidth="1* 1* 2*">
                <sthead>
                  <stentry>Field</stentry>
                  <stentry>Type</stentry>
                  <stentry>Description</stentry>
                </sthead>
                <strow>
                  <stentry><codeph>documents</codeph></stentry>
                  <stentry>string[]</stentry>
                  <stentry>List of absolute paths or URLs of the documents whose changes were
                    rejected.</stentry>
                </strow>
              </simpletable>
            </dd>
          </dlentry>
          
      </dl></p>
    </section>
    <note id="note_hooks_version">The <codeph>AIHooksHandler</codeph> extension point is available
      starting with version 28.0 of <ph keyref="product"/>.</note>
  </body>
</topic>
